{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/pulls/25046","id":5078904325,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAB0Los8AAAABLrnuBQ","html_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/pull/25046","diff_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/pull/25046.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/pull/25046.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/25046","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/pulls/25046/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/pulls/25046/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/25046/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/statuses/5089bcc83c8193e6a965dd1579767b1d503401ba","number":25046,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix GH-24792: Assignment-result writes compile but fail with invalid opcode","user":{"login":"ChrisAbner","id":48162172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTYyMTcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48162172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner","html_url":"https://github.com/ChrisAbner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes GH-24792.\n\nSince the VAR|TMP overhaul (6173a9a109), `zend_compile_var_inner()` compiles `ZEND_AST_ASSIGN` and `ZEND_AST_ASSIGN_REF` for every fetch type. When an assignment is the container of a write, such as `($a = [1])[0] = 2`, `unset(($a = [1])[0])` or `$r = &($a = [1])[0]`, the compiler emits a write fetch on the TMP result of the assignment. That combination has no handler, so the script compiles and then dies with `Invalid opcode`. PHP 8.5 rejected all of these at compile time with \"Cannot use temporary expression in write context\". This patch restores that error.\n\nThe overhaul added these cases so that a destructuring assignment with references can be passed by reference (`f([&$x] = $arr)`). It originally had an assertion limiting them to that case, which a01a8e72ac removed. The patch keeps compiling assignments when `by_ref` is set or when the fetch is not a write (`W`/`RW`/`UNSET`), and otherwise falls through to the existing `default` branch and its error. This puts the check in the one place every write container goes through. Checking in each caller (dim, prop, unset, inc/dec, reference fetch) would have needed one check per caller. As a side effect, `($a =& $b)[0] = 2` and `([&$x] = $arr)[0] = 5` are compile errors again. PHP 8.5 rejected them too; 8.6.0RC4 started executing them. If you would rather keep those working in 8.6, I can narrow the check.\n\n**Verification.** Debug NTS build of `PHP-8.6` (e2fa0c9f7f, `--disable-all --enable-cli`), compared with the official `php:8.5-cli` (8.5.12) and `php:8.6.0RC4-cli` images:\n\n| Code | 8.5.12 | 8.6.0RC4 | PHP-8.6 + patch |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `($a = [1])[0] = 2;` | compile error | `Invalid opcode 23/2/1` | compile error |\n| `($a = new stdClass)->p = 1;` | compile error | `Invalid opcode 24/2/1` | compile error |\n| `($a = [1])[0] += 2;` | compile error | `Invalid opcode 27/2/1` | compile error |\n| `($a = [1])[0]++;` | compile error | `Invalid opcode 87/2/1` | compile error |\n| `unset(($a = [1])[0]);` | compile error | `Invalid opcode 75/2/1` | compile error |\n| `$r = &($a = [1])[0];` | compile error | `Invalid opcode 84/2/1` | compile error |\n| `f(($a = [1])[0]);` with `f(&$x)` | compile error | `Invalid opcode 84/2/1` | compile error |\n| `($a =& $b)[0] = 2;` | compile error | runs | compile error |\n| `([&$x] = $arr)[0] = 5;` | compile error | runs | compile error |\n| `f([&$x] = $arr);` / `f($a =& $b);` with `f(&$x)` | works | works | works |\n| `isset(($a = [1])[0])`, `($a = [1])[5] ?? 'd'`, `($v = ['k' => 'v'])['k']` | works | works | works |\n\nOut of 30 variants in total, all 30 match 8.5.12 with the patch, with and without OPcache + tracing JIT. Without the patch, 15 fail with `Invalid opcode` in 8.6.0RC4 and on master.\n\n| Tests | Result |\n|---|---|\n| New `Zend/tests/gh24792*.phpt` (9) on 8.5.12 / 8.6.0RC4 / patched | 9 pass / 8 fail / 9 pass |\n| `Zend/tests` + `tests`, patched | 6301 passed, 0 failed |\n| `Zend/tests` + `tests` + `ext/opcache/tests`, patched, `opcache.enable_cli=1`, `opcache.jit=tracing`, `opcache.protect_memory=1` | 7275 passed, 0 failed |\n\nNot covered: `foreach (($a =& $b) as &$v) { $v = 3; }` writes through to `$b` in 8.5 but not in 8.6.0RC4, with or without this patch. It is a separate behaviour change from the same overhaul and is left alone here. I only tested on Linux x86_64 NTS debug builds, not ZTS or ASAN builds of the patch. The bug itself also reproduces on the official ZTS RC4 image.\n","labels":[{"id":3045702973,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMDQ1NzAyOTcz","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/labels/Category:%20Engine","name":"Category: Engine","description":"","color":"5319E7","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-30T03:14:11Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T22:36:56Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"ChrisAbner:fix-gh-24792","ref":"fix-gh-24792","repo":{"id":1438832199,"node_id":"R_kgDOVcLWRw","name":"php-src","full_name":"ChrisAbner/php-src","owner":{"login":"ChrisAbner","id":48162172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTYyMTcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48162172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner","html_url":"https://github.com/ChrisAbner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":true,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"The PHP Interpreter","homepage":"https://www.php.net","language":null,"visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":[],"forks_count":0,"forks":0,"stargazers_count":0,"watchers_count":0,"watchers":0,"open_issues_count":0,"open_issues":0,"size":660206,"default_branch":"master","has_issues":false,"has_projects":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_downloads":false,"has_discussions":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pushed_at":"2026-11-19T18:31:19Z","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:50:55Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T18:50:55Z","allow_forking":true,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","license":{"key":"bsd-3-clause","name":"BSD 3-Clause \"New\" or \"Revised\" License","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/bsd-3-clause","spdx_id":"BSD-3-Clause","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTU="},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ChrisAbner/php-src","html_url":"https://github.com/Chr